Source landscape: the 2023 Egypt document universe for Chapter 7B is dominated by official presidential/gazette material, election-competition records, U.S./UN human-rights reporting, major NGO annual reports, and a smaller but useful set of academic and investigative pieces on corruption, public trust, appointments, pardons, procurement, and the New Administrative Capital. I found enough variety to exceed the 30-document discovery floor; a few items are restricted or metadata-only and should be carried forward as candidates.

